  "Notes": "Two-layer quarter-wave beam divider (MgF2 then TiO2 on glass)\nSpecification: All layers quarter-wave at 550 nm; maximise reflectance with low loss.\nReported: Table p. 338: R = 50.0 %, T = 49.5 % at 550 nm.\nNotes: The table lists the films from the glass outward ('Film materials on glass', TiO2 always last as the top film, cf. text p. 338 'especially suitable as a top film'), so the list is reversed here. MgF2 n = 1.38 is the paper's nD value used as a constant. Ideal QW calculation with these constants gives R = 50.0 % at 550 nm, matching the table.\nLayers from Table on p. 338 (row 'MgF2 - TiO2'), text p. 338 ('With quarter wave-length thick films of these materials ... on glass with ng = 1.51 at lambda = 550 millimicrons'); layer 1 faces the incident medium.\nChecked with ThinFilmDesigner (2026-10-21), agrees with the paper: ours R 50.0 % at 550 nm; paper R 50 % (measured, table p. 338).",
